A||||6||Blaster||Engine compartment liner...||||5||
Z||000000||Blaster||07-26-2000||04:28 AM||||I was wondering what the point of that engine compartment liner stuff was.  I can understand it being on the firewall,  but why on the side walls of the compartment?  Was it part of the fire prevention thing?  Also, I have seen many pictures of cars where that stuff has been removed.  I have my motor out right now and the stuff looks really raggedy, so I was wondering if it would matter if I removed it.  Any input would be appreciated.  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||07-26-2000||05:06 AM||||Mainly just insulation, from what I understand.  I haven't heard of any problems occuring from taking it off, and the engine compartment looks a lot cleaner without it.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||07-26-2000||09:03 AM||||It's fiberglass,so if you don't like to get all itchy when you work on your car,there's another reason to remove it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||07-26-2000||12:51 PM||||Why did they put insulation in the engine compartment??  It should keep it cooler without it.....<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||5
Z||000004||webbee||07-26-2000||02:48 PM||||On the firewall I think it's to keep heat from the ecm and pass compartment. Don't know why on sides. It's fiberglass, which has little sound reduction ability, so it must be heat related . Since GM is cost driven and they could save lots of $ per unit by not installing it, the engineers must have had a pretty good reason for it being there. For that reason alone I would not remove it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||07-27-2000||05:39 PM||||actually it is MORE for soundproofing than anything else. Take it all out and pitch it. on the sides it also allows for more fresh air holes to be uncovered. theres a big hole beside battery to let in tons of fresh air. cant hurt keeping the battery cooler either. Youll only notice slightly more noise coming thru but if your like me, the sound of a sweet running engine is music. <P>rg||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||07-27-2000||11:08 PM||||Mine's been removed on the sides for 5 years.  No problems here.||||reg||1
